      "end": 58.75866666666667,
      "lesson_progress": 0.3333333333333333,
      "text": "Multiples are products formed by multiplying a number by whole numbers. Adding another equal group produces the next positive multiple. The list continues without ending; zero is also a multiple, although our counting patterns start at the first positive one. Picture three groups of six counters. Each new group adds six more counters.",
      "chapter": "Build the idea",
